{"commit": "9dc8075dd1b96d3a2744717a9d6d98a3024acbec", "subject": "[T-001] Implement immutable statistics and whole-text counting", "closed": ["T-001"], "single_matching_closure": true, "changed_paths": [".gitignore", "AGENTS.md", "README.md", "docs/dev/TASKS.md", "tests/__init__.py", "tests/integration/__init__.py", "tests/integration/test_api.py", "tests/unit/__init__.py", "tests/unit/test_core.py", "textstats/__init__.py", "textstats/core.py"], "evidence": ["+## T-001 completion evidence", "+After implementing the contracts, `python -m unittest discover -s tests/unit -t . -v` passed all 10 tests and `python -m unittest discover -s tests/integration -t . -v` passed all 5 tests, without skips or warnings. Evidence covers every whole-input SPEC matrix row under both policies; Unicode separators/whitespace and non-ASCII words; mixed/consecutive/final terminators; repeated/interior BOMs; equality, invalid fields and assignment/deletion immutability; direct exports/signatures, keyword-only policy, repeated-call independence and import/call silence. Verification also inspects source/document contracts and preserved internal segment seams. Coverage is T-001 on this runtime, not full Python-version, file/API, CLI or distribution acceptance. The future check tools are absent because their owning tasks are unselected.", "+Exactly T-001's result, tests, documentation, current evidence and initial checkbox close together in its task commit. Publication and issue closure are subsequent observed operations reported in the workflow handoff. All parents and T-002 through T-017 remain unchecked. Stop after the verified push and hosted reconciliation of T-001; do not integrate the incomplete phase or start another task."]}
{"commit": "f28f6e415b3e0c13353a61e82354c47b0d2cabb2", "subject": "[T-002] Implement strict file acquisition and complete public API", "closed": ["T-002"], "single_matching_closure": true, "changed_paths": ["docs/dev/TASKS.md", "tests/integration/test_api.py", "tests/unit/test_io.py", "textstats/__init__.py", "textstats/io.py"], "evidence": ["+## T-002 completion evidence", "+The milestone 1.1 request selects T-002 through T-004 and supersedes historical first-task/preparation stops only within this boundary. Startup clean branch/remote tip was `9dc8075dd1b96d3a2744717a9d6d98a3024acbec`; its T-001 result/evidence/initial checkbox and single-ID subject were inspected and compliant. Accepted preparation remains published on main `88a5c4b4424f4bba76940e40b1d6523b1f6fe191`. Current SPEC/PLAN/layout and adjacent Ready owner reviews retain unchanged governing contracts; TASKS differs only in T-001 completion evidence/status, which does not invalidate hierarchy QC. Maintained phase tracking readback returned the phase label, milestones 1\u20133 and unique marked T-001\u2013T-009 issues 2\u201310 with correct parent associations before task edits/tests. T-002 maps uniquely to issue #3, milestone #1; T-001 issue #2 is closed.", "+Tests preceded production behavior. With an unimplemented count_file declaration (so import/collection was valid), `python -m unittest discover -s tests/unit -t . -v` collected 14 tests and failed with six behavioral NotImplementedError errors at the acquisition scenarios; the ten core tests stayed green. After production implementation, that command passed 14 tests and `python -m unittest discover -s tests/integration -t . -v` passed 8 tests on Python 3.12.14 without skips or warnings. Coverage includes controlled success/read/decode/open failures and closed handles, PermissionError/FileNotFoundError/IsADirectoryError propagation, real-file strict decode and missing path, all whole-input matrix rows under both policies using str and Path arguments, Unicode content, exact byte preservation, direct exports/signature and API silence. Source and docstring inspection confirms no CLI dependency or fallback decoding. No TDD exception; broader CLI/distribution and other runtimes remain unverified. Exactly this task's result/tests/documentation/evidence/initial checkbox close together before publication and issue reconciliation; remaining milestone tasks and all parents stay open."]}
{"commit": "373203d6f41bee2229eed900b761de8669678e0b", "subject": "[T-003] Integrate named-file CLI and nonempty product checks", "closed": ["T-003"], "single_matching_closure": true, "changed_paths": ["AGENTS.md", "README.md", "docs/dev/TASKS.md", "tests/integration/test_cli.py", "tests/unit/test_cli.py", "textstats/__main__.py", "textstats/cli.py", "tools/check_tests.py"], "evidence": ["+## T-003 completion evidence", "+T-002 was closed durably at `f28f6e415b3e0c13353a61e82354c47b0d2cabb2`, pushed and read back as exact remote phase tip before T-003 work. Provider readback confirms its issue #3 closed/completed with the evidence comment; recovery after an overbroad Link-header guard independently read actual closed state and the existing comment without duplicating writes. T-003 uniquely maps to maintained issue #4, milestone #1.", "+Tests preceded behavior. `python -m unittest tests.unit.test_cli -v` collected seven tests and failed with four assertions and five NotImplementedError errors against unimplemented CLI and a runner that incorrectly returned success without discovery. These are observed behavioral RED failures, including both empty-suite rejection and propagation of a product failure. `python tools/check_tests.py` subsequently passed 21 unit and 12 integration tests on Python 3.12.14, without skips/warnings. The runner reports independent counts, rejects zero in either suite, executes both real product suites and propagates failure. Its subprocess fixtures exercise empty unit, empty integration, failure propagation, successful independent counts and exclusion of deliberately failing workflow fixtures."]}
{"commit": "7d003c1cf31c994340d8644e95990ef2253754ed", "subject": "[T-004] Review named-file counting and complete milestone 1.1", "closed": ["T-004"], "single_matching_closure": true, "changed_paths": ["docs/dev/TASKS.md", "docs/dev/reports/phases/1/1.1.md"], "evidence": ["+            Report: [milestone 1.1 review](reports/phases/1/1.1.md).", "+## T-004 completion evidence", "+Completed the separate coherent milestone implementation code review, actual nonempty runner, API/module demonstration and exit assessment in [milestone 1.1 report](reports/phases/1/1.1.md), reviewed at published T-003 source `373203d6f41bee2229eed900b761de8669678e0b`. The runner passed 21 unit and 12 integration tests on Python 3.12.14, with no skips/warnings. Mixed-terminator/non-ASCII/BOM temporary-file API and real CLI returned three lines/four words with exact streams/status and unchanged bytes; BOM-only default versus retaining calls visibly produced zero/zero versus one/one. Source review found no milestone contract blocker and no required repair; TODO is None. Full runtime/platform matrix, complete CLI failure diagnostics, public guide/distribution and later phase capabilities remain unverified/planned in their owning tasks.", "+T-002/T-003 separate closing commits were inspected and published before this review; provider readback confirms issues #3/#4 closed/completed with evidence, and T-001 #2 remains closed. Unique T-004 issue is #5 in native milestone #1. The report/evidence, initial T-004 checkbox and eligible milestone 1.1 parent close together; phase and unselected tasks remain unchecked. Publish/read back this task commit before closing issue #5, then validate all milestone-associated task issues and close/read back milestone #1. Stop on the incomplete phase branch, with main unchanged and no release or T-005 work."]}
{"commit": "809f045e3cd32445e7dca29d0174ea25aa5da7ea", "subject": "[T-005] Handle named-file input failures without tracebacks", "closed": ["T-005"], "single_matching_closure": true, "changed_paths": ["docs/dev/TASKS.md", "tests/integration/test_cli.py", "tests/unit/test_cli.py", "textstats/cli.py"], "evidence": ["+## T-005 completion evidence", "+The complete-phase request selects T-005 through T-009 and explicit full-phase integration, superseding the historical Phase 1 partial stops. Startup published phase tip `7d003c1cf31c994340d8644e95990ef2253754ed` and main `88a5c4b4424f4bba76940e40b1d6523b1f6fe191` were read back exactly; latest T-004 closing result/report/evidence/initial checkbox composition is compliant. Current SPEC/PLAN/layout hashes match the accepted Ready owner reports, and TASKS changes only completion/evidence, preserving reviewed hierarchy/contracts. Provider readback verified all nine uniquely marked Phase 1 task issues #2\u2013#10 with phase label and milestones #1\u2013#3, and T-001\u2013T-004 issues plus milestone #1 closed. T-005 uniquely maps to #6 in milestone #2; unrelated hosted material is retained.", "+Tests preceded the production change. `python -m unittest tests.unit.test_cli.CliTests tests.integration.test_cli -v` ran 12 tests with four errors and four failures: expected controlled FileNotFoundError/PermissionError/read OSError/decode errors escaped, real module missing-file failures exposed tracebacks and bad-byte failures omitted the input identity. These are meaningful behavioral RED. Usage-before-acquisition cases already passed. The CLI now catches only expected OSError/UnicodeDecodeError, emits identifying input/cause stderr, returns 1 and leaves stdout empty. Parsing precedes acquisition and retains status 2, success/help/BOM/dash-file contracts and silent API exceptions.", "+`python tools/check_tests.py` passed 23 unit and 14 integration tests on Python 3.12.14, no skips/warnings; `git diff --check` passed. Controlled open/read/decode/owned-handle checks and CLI failures, real subprocess missing/bad-byte inputs under both BOM policies, invocation errors before acquisition, exact success/help streams, API semantics and unchanged bytes are covered. Source/docstring inspection found no scoped contract blocker. Broader runtime/platform coverage, public guide and distribution remain later selected tasks; Phase 2 stays unselected. Result/tests/source documentation/current evidence and initial T-005 checkbox close together before publication and issue #6 reconciliation."]}
{"commit": "fde1537b5c4ba1bcef4f538dfb47276d564e4aaa", "subject": "[T-006] Document public API and runnable named-file usage", "closed": ["T-006"], "single_matching_closure": true, "changed_paths": ["AGENTS.md", "README.md", "docs/dev/TASKS.md", "docs/public-api.md"], "evidence": ["+## T-006 completion evidence", "+T-005 closing commit `809f045e3cd32445e7dca29d0174ea25aa5da7ea` was pushed and exact remote containment verified before documentation work; provider issue #6 is closed/completed with evidence. T-006 maps uniquely to #7, milestone #2. Delivered [public API/module reference](../public-api.md), runnable README setup/named-file/API/BOM/help/check examples, precise constructor/signature/counting/decode/exception/ownership/silence contracts and module responsibility navigation. Source docstrings were inspected against the guide and already satisfy the delivered boundaries. Root AGENTS retains controlling instructions and now reflects the authorized complete-phase stop and real public guide. Distribution is explicitly planned pending T-007; JSON/stdin/ranges are not advertised as delivered.", "+Every runnable bash/Python fence in README and the public guide was executed verbatim in repository context on Python 3.12.14. The sample produced exact `lines=3 words=5`, BOM default/retaining produced zero/zero and one/one, dash-file produced one/two, help succeeded, and silent API assertions passed. Runner and separate documented discover commands each passed 23 unit and 14 integration tests with no skips/warnings. Local user-guide links resolve; changed diff whitespace passed. Temporary example inputs were cleaned. This documentation-only task adds no behavioral code and requires no fabricated RED cycle; existing source coverage supports the inspected contracts. External notice links and other runtimes were not revalidated. Documentation/navigation/evidence/initial checkbox close together before publication and issue #7 reconciliation."]}
{"commit": "f7e3309b672cb13b1d8158613e81d50e8d1ecc18", "subject": "[T-007] Build and verify isolated TextStats source distribution", "closed": ["T-007"], "single_matching_closure": true, "changed_paths": [".gitignore", "AGENTS.md", "README.md", "docs/dev/TASKS.md", "tests/integration/test_distribution.py", "tools/check_distribution.py", "tools/package_source.py"], "evidence": ["+## T-007 completion evidence", "+Tests preceded production functionality. With valid importable NotImplementedError declarations, `python -m unittest tests.integration.test_distribution -v` ran four tests and failed with three errors and one assertion failure, demonstrating absent packaging and checker behavior. Source review corrected the controlled faulty-archive test's CLI path before implementation; no false sensitivity claim is made for that earlier fixture. After implementation, the same four tests passed, including exact content/byte allowlist under harmless unrelated-file pollution, checkout-PYTHONPATH pollution and rejection of a deliberately wrong extracted CLI while the checkout remains healthy. No copied real credential enters a fixture.", "+`python tools/check_tests.py` passed 23 unit and 18 integration tests on Python 3.12.14, no skips/warnings. `python tools/check_distribution.py` verified exact extracted import path and 35 actual `python -s -m textstats` invocations from temporary extracted cwd with inherited PYTHONPATH/PYTHONHOME removed and user-site packages disabled: fourteen semantic/Unicode/terminator/BOM cases under both policies, dash-file success, missing/decode failures, three usage errors and help. Exact success/status/streams, input identity/cause/no traceback and unchanged sample/bad/dash bytes were verified; temporary extractions clean up on failure too. The checker builds an ignored archive and imports no checkout product code for acceptance.", "+Every updated README/public-guide runnable fence, including builder/checker and a separate Bash extraction/example, executed successfully. The extracted example returned exact three lines/five words; checkout-only test commands are explicitly distinguished from archive tools. Local user-guide links and diff whitespace passed. Other runtimes/platforms, locale-varied stdin, JSON/ranges, installed packaging and release publication remain unverified/outside Phase 1. Result/tests/docs/evidence/initial checkbox close together before publication and issue #8 reconciliation."]}
{"commit": "7b9f570aa4452d2ca9d6105479640528cb113f0e", "subject": "[T-008] Review distribution milestone and reject option abbreviations", "closed": ["T-008"], "single_matching_closure": true, "changed_paths": ["README.md", "docs/dev/TASKS.md", "docs/dev/reports/phases/1/1.2.md", "tests/integration/test_cli.py", "tests/unit/test_cli.py", "textstats/cli.py", "tools/check_distribution.py"], "evidence": ["+            Report: [milestone 1.2 review](reports/phases/1/1.2.md).", "+## T-008 completion evidence", "+`python tools/check_tests.py` passed 23 unit and 18 integration tests on Python 3.12.14 without skips/warnings; `python tools/check_distribution.py` verified isolated extracted import and 36 actual module processes. Current source review found no remaining milestone blocker, docs/examples retain applicable executed evidence and TODO is None. T-005\u2013T-007 commits were separately published/read back and issues #6\u2013#8 closed before this review. T-008 uniquely maps to issue #9/milestone #2. Report, scoped repair/tests/docs, evidence, initial task checkbox and eligible milestone parent status close together; publish/read back before review issue closure and milestone #2 validation/closure. Phase review remains unchecked until that hosted gate succeeds."]}
{"commit": "5b17e4650c64c7c735991931b591bdabb8069215", "subject": "[T-009] Review and complete Phase 1 named-file utility exits", "closed": ["T-009"], "single_matching_closure": true, "changed_paths": ["AGENTS.md", "docs/dev/TASKS.md", "docs/dev/reports/phases/1/PHASE-REPORT.md"], "evidence": ["+            Report: [phase 1 review](reports/phases/1/PHASE-REPORT.md).", "+## T-009 completion evidence", "+Fresh product runner passed 23 unit and 18 integration tests on Python 3.12.14, no skips/warnings. Fresh extraction checker verified exact isolated import and 36 real module cases. Every current README/public-guide runnable fence, including separate extracted example, passed; documented discovery counts are nonzero, outputs are exact and user-guide links resolve. Complete branch-scope inspection retains coordinator resources/pinned package/publisher fixture unchanged. Bounded T-001\u2013T-008 actual parent-diff audit confirms per-task result/evidence/initial checkbox composition and leading single owning IDs. T-009 report/evidence/initial task checkbox and eligible phase/review-milestone parent status close together, followed by verified publication and hosted issue/review-milestone closure. Then integrate the complete phase via explicit two-parent merge, verify merged state and publish/read back main; integration evidence belongs in that actual merge summary. Stop before Phase 2; all T-010\u2013T-017 remain unchecked/unprojected. Broader runtime/platform matrix and release remain outside scope."]}

